<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="017" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-11: Approval on the Decide lane: intake approval Signal, claim, approve-intake / reject-intake plan actions, review Decision Record, approved SPE versions, resume from AwaitingApproval</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after:013,010,014</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and auth; changes the Signals subject set, the decision commit route's guards and Signal/Decision Record readers; new claim write and executors.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-sensitive and cross-project: fail-closed authorization on the step that releases AI output (NFR-02), plus ontology-owned Services/Signals code reviewed by ontology-r1 (D-115) and access reviewed by uac-r2.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with 023 and 024 on EndpointMappingExtensions.cs; with 014 on JobProcessingModule.cs (014 is merged first).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 010, 014</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, auth, authorization, dataverse, signals</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement intake approval on the existing Decide lane (owner decision 2026-11-28, notes/decisions.md rows "Intake approval runs on the Decide lane" and "Decide-lane approval: conditions agreed"). When a run reaches Approve, the request's stage becomes Awaiting approval and the orchestrator raises an intake Signal-evaluation trigger. An intake approval policy (Decide lane, subject `sprk_servicerequest`, rule: the intake stage is Awaiting approval, scoped to intake rows) then raises ONE Decide-lane Signal, the Work Item, through the existing evaluate-plan-write path. Its plan offers two catalog actions, `approve-intake` and `reject-intake`, committed through `DecisionCommitService`, which writes the review-kind Decision Record. Claim is intake's own action: it sets the assigned attorney through the existing Assigned-To write path. Approve records each output's current SPE version, moves the run to Approved and enqueues Return. Reject ends the run (not Failed) and returns the request to In review. Authorization fails closed at every step. Do NOT add a new DecisionRecordWriter kind and do NOT use `IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync`.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, endpoint-filter authorization, Dataverse write paths, ADR-004 idempotency and the ontology Signals / decision-commit model. Follow ADRs and the agreed conditions literally.</role>
  <goal>An intake approval appears as one Decide-lane Work Item per run, visible only to callers who can read the request. It can be claimed by one owning-team member and approved or rejected by the claimer through the decision commit route. The Decision Record is written for both outcomes. Return is enqueued exactly once on approve. Every agreed guard has must-fire and must-not-fire tests.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-11, NFR-01/02/08. Owner decisions 2026-11-28 (notes/decisions.md): Decide lane over a To Do; authorization "Team, then claimer"; self-approval ALLOWED (the requester may claim and approve if they pass the checks, so there is no separation-of-duties bar, and one test pins this); kill switch = the run's harness switch. ontology-r1 accepted changes to their code on this branch, with their review before merge (D-115). uac-r2 set the access conditions. Both sets are copied into the constraints below. Run state, the Return job and the intake options come from 013; engine completion from 014; request columns from 010 (`sprk_intakestage` Awaiting approval = 100000003, In review = 100000001; assigned attorney = `sprk_assignedtointernal` → contact via `ContactUserRepresentation.ResolveContactForUserAsync`).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs (VerifiedSubjects :516; DueDateColumnBySubject stays unset for sprk_servicerequest)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/PredicateCompiler.cs (EvaluatorGlobalReadableEntities :198; only after the live check in step 2)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalEvaluationTriggerHandler.cs (SignalTriggerKind: add IntakeAwaitingApproval; IncludesDoLane false)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionCatalog.cs (approve-intake / reject-intake; pattern: approve-variance :243)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/Actions/DecisionActionExecutors.cs (executor: PreflightAsync + ExecuteAsync)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs (dismissal and Also-resolve refusals for the intake policy, ~:1721)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalReadService.cs and DecisionCapability.cs (service-request subject authorised by the caller's rights on the request; unknown subject type fails closed)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeApprovalService.cs (claim / approve / reject transitions)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalEndpoints.cs (claim route; the model-driven form's approve/reject entry calls the same decision commit route, never a second writer)</file>
