  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner-2026-11-28">SCOPE = the whole task. No new DecisionRecordWriter kind, no `IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync`, no direct `SignalWriter.WriteAsync` call from intake: the Signal is raised only by the evaluate-plan-write path (`SignalEvaluationTrigger` → re-evaluation), with the nightly pass as backstop.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (a)1">SCOPE = subject allow-lists. Add `sprk_servicerequest` to `SignalWriter.VerifiedSubjects`. Add it to `PredicateCompiler.EvaluatorGlobalReadableEntities` ONLY after the live check (PredicateCompiler remarks §9.2: the same rows as admin and as the ontology writer) shows the writer reads it at Global depth. If that needs a privilege on the Spaarke Ontology Service role, STOP: a role edit needs the owner's approval.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (a)2">SCOPE = the rule body and every read. Outbound inquiries (`sprk_direction` = Outbound) live in the same table. The rule selects intake rows explicitly (`sprk_intakestage` = Awaiting approval, plus direction if a stage can be set on an inquiry). InquiryDispositionService, the ClosesTodo open-inquiry guard and the InquiryDisposition trigger are unchanged. The message template names only TemplateEligibleFields (PolicyVersionValidator).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (a)3">SCOPE = the trigger. New `SignalTriggerKind.IntakeAwaitingApproval`, routed through `SignalEvaluationTrigger` (never throws; key `signal-eval-{kind}-{subjectId}-{sourceId}`; IncludesDoLane false). If the stage moves without a decision, the re-evaluation closes the Signal ConditionCleared.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (a)4">SCOPE = catalog. Codes `approve-intake` and `reject-intake` (kebab-case, Decide lane): mutual Excludes (FirstConflict), a Gate, RecordClass Judgement, ResolvesSignal true. A new Decide WorkType value ("approve") requires checking how the Console Decide lane groups and labels work types (src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/**); if the UI does not handle it, report and do not ship a blank label. Catalog, describer and plan text are pinned in contract baselines: run `--filter "FullyQualifiedName~Signals"` and update `tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/Baselines` (plan.200.*.json) in this change (#3016).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (a)5 / D-129">SCOPE = ownership. The claimer/decider is a person column (`sprk_assignedtointernal`, a contact), never ownerid. Registering that column for sprk_servicerequest in RecordTableRules / OwnedChildWrite.ForPersonColumns, and the secure-child status of Signals and Decision Records on a Secure request (D-33/D-123), follow uac-r2's direction; if the needed rule is unclear, STOP and ask through the main session.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (b)">SCOPE = executors. The claimer and record checks are implemented in the executor's `PreflightAsync` (runs as the caller before any write; `DecisionActionReasons.NotAuthorized` → 403; other codes → 409-class refusal) AND re-checked in `ExecuteAsync`. IntakeApprovalService's transition is conditional (stage still Awaiting approval, same claimer, If-Match on the row), so a race refuses instead of approving twice. The executor is idempotent on retry: the Return enqueue key is deterministic (`intake-return:{runId:N}`, the 013 key).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 (c)">SCOPE = DecisionCommitService. For the intake approval policy: refuse dismissal with a reason code and never count it toward suppression (D-11); refuse intake-approval Signals as Also-resolve targets of any other decision; refuse Also-resolve on the intake item itself. All three are checked before the first write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 (a) / owner 'Team, then claimer'">SCOPE = every claim, approve and reject. Checks in this order, each as the caller and fail closed. (1) Record check: the caller's own rights on the sprk_servicerequest through the equalised gate question (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsForAuthorizationGateAsync`): Read for every action, Write for claim, approve and reject. A fail, a fault, an unknown id or a non-intake row all give the SAME 404 (byte-identical body apart from the correlation id). (2) Membership of the request's owning team through `IIdentityNormalizationService.ResolveAsync(...).TeamIds`; a non-member gets 403; a fault or an unresolved team gets 403; the 2-minute cache is named as a K-class limit in the PR. (3) After a claim, only the claimer may approve or reject (403). Re-run (1)–(3) at approve and reject time, not only at claim. Self-approval is allowed (owner): the requester is not barred, and one test pins it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 (b)">SCOPE = Signal and Decision Record readers (list and by id: SignalReadService, DecisionCapability, the Decide page, the MCP decision tools). A service-request subject is authorised by the caller's rights on that request. A subject table a reader does not know fails closed, never "no restriction". These Signals and Decision Records never reach a contact, the External SPA or any external surface (task 028 rule).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 (c) / ADR-002 / ADR-034">SCOPE = claim. Through the existing Assigned-To write path (one owner per invariant; keeps the ADR-034 A4 Collaborate grant and notifications in step), self-assignment only, conditional on the row version (If-Match), so two simultaneous claims give exactly one winner and one 409. G5: check as the user, write as the app; the Decision Record carries the person in `sprk_createdbyperson`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 / owner">SCOPE = claim, approve, reject. The run's harness switch (`IntakePipelineOptions.IsHarnessEnabled(harnessKey)`) is checked AFTER authorization; off → 503 `INTAKE_DISABLED` and nothing is written (prove it in a test). No new switch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-019">SCOPE = the claim route and any intake route. Endpoint filter + `.RequireAuthorization()`; ProblemDetails with stable codes (INTAKE_RUN_NOT_FOUND, INTAKE_FORBIDDEN, INTAKE_RUN_WRONG_STATE, INTAKE_ALREADY_CLAIMED, INTAKE_DISABLED) and the correlation id.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SCOPE = approved-version capture: the current SPE version id of each output document, through `SpeFileStore` (GetCurrentVersionIdAsync) only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = all logs, ProblemDetails, Signal text and Decision Record text written here: identifiers only; a reject reason is stored on the Decision Record and never logged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10/§11">SCOPE = BFF changes. Placement Justification and §11 answers per new surface in the report; no new package or HIGH CVE; the main session measures publish size.</constraint>
    <constraint source="public-repo">SCOPE = commit messages, notes, test names visible in PR text. No environment ids, identity ids or access-control mechanics (ontology-r1 / uac-r2); describe areas only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

