  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Load the knowledge files, the 013/014 intake code and the Signals code listed above; declare RIGOR FULL, tier opus, effort high.</step>
    <step order="2">Live read-only check: does the ontology writer identity read sprk_servicerequest at Global depth (PredicateCompiler §9.2 method)? This is a read; do it only if it needs no new privilege or secret, otherwise report what is needed and continue with the code behind the allow-list change, unmerged into the allow-list.</step>
    <step order="3">Subject + rule + trigger: VerifiedSubjects; the trigger kind; the orchestrator's Approve stage sets the stage and enqueues the trigger (idempotent); the policy/version seed script (not run).</step>
    <step order="4">Catalog actions + executor (preflight + execute) + IntakeApprovalService (conditional transitions, version capture, Return enqueue, run close on reject).</step>
    <step order="5">DecisionCommitService refusals (dismissal, Also-resolve both ways) and the reader gating for service-request subjects (fail closed, never external).</step>
    <step order="6">Claim route through the Assigned-To write path; the model-driven form's approve/reject entry point calls the decision commit route.</step>
    <step order="7">Tests (see criteria), `--filter "FullyQualifiedName~Signals"` with baselines updated, the Intake filter, full `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests`, `dotnet build` 0 warnings.</step>
    <step order="8">Document deviations in projects/spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1/notes/017-approval.md. Do not edit TASK-INDEX.md or current-task.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The live check shows the ontology writer cannot read sprk_servicerequest at Global depth without a role privilege change: STOP that part and report (owner approval needed).</trigger>
    <trigger>The commit route cannot refuse dismissal or Also-resolve per policy without changing behaviour for existing policies: STOP and report the options.</trigger>
    <trigger>The Assigned-To write path cannot do a conditional (If-Match) self-assignment on sprk_servicerequest, or uac-r2's person-column registration rule is unclear: STOP and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>The Console Decide lane cannot show a new WorkType without UI work: report it (UI change is task 019's scope), do not hack a label.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The Decide lane (SignalWriter, SignalEvaluationTrigger, DecisionActionCatalog, DecisionCommitService, the review-kind DecisionRecordWriter path) owns Work Items and decisions (ontology-component-model.md: "Work queue = things not yet decided. Decision Record = things decided"). The Assigned-To write path owns sprk_assignedtointernal.</existing>
    <extension>Yes: everything except IntakeApprovalService and the claim route extends existing components (a subject, a trigger kind, two catalog entries, one executor, three commit refusals, reader gating).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Runs needing approval stay in AwaitingApproval forever; FR-11, FR-13(b) and Return never happen.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">The modified Signals files, IntakeApprovalService.cs, IntakeApprovalEndpoints.cs, the Approve-stage change in IntakeRunJobHandler.cs, scripts/intake/Apply-IntakeApprovalPolicy.ps1</output>
    <output type="test">The four test files listed in relevant-files, plus updated Signals contract baselines</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A run reaching Approve sets the request stage to Awaiting approval and enqueues one IntakeAwaitingApproval trigger; evaluating it raises exactly one Decide-lane Signal on the request, owned by the request's owning team; redelivering the stage or the trigger raises no second Signal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The rule never selects an outbound inquiry row or a row with a null intake stage; the inquiry paths' existing tests pass unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Claim by an owning-team member with Read+Write on the request sets the assigned attorney to the caller's contact through the Assigned-To path; a second claim by someone else → 409 INTAKE_ALREADY_CLAIMED, nothing changed; two simultaneous claims → exactly one winner and one 409.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The claimer's approve-intake commit returns success, writes one review-kind Decision Record (approved, sprk_createdbyperson = the caller), records the approved SPE version ids, moves the run to Approved, resolves the Signal and enqueues one Return job (key intake-return:{runId:N}); a repeated or retried commit writes no second record or Return job.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The claimer's reject-intake commit writes one Decision Record (rejected), ends the run (not Failed), sets the request stage to In review and resolves the Signal.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Self-approval (owner "Allow it"; ontology D-237: being the requester is no bar and grants nothing): must-not-fire, the requester who is an owning-team member and passes the record checks can claim and approve; must-fire, a requester WITHOUT approval rights (not in the team, or no Write) is refused (NotAuthorized → 403, or the 404 of the record check) before any write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative, each with a test and mutation evidence for the record and claimer checks: unknown id and no-Read caller and No Access on a secure request → identical 404; non-member → 403; non-claimer after a claim → 403 (from PreflightAsync, and again when the claim changes between preflight and execute); a caller who lost membership or rights after claiming → refused at approve/reject; no token → 401.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Harness switch off → 503 INTAKE_DISABLED for claim, approve and reject, after authorization (an unauthorised caller still gets 404/403), and nothing is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Dismissal of the intake Signal is refused with a reason code and counts toward no suppression; an intake Signal cannot be an Also-resolve target of another decision; Also-resolve on the intake item is refused; each before any write, with must-not-fire tests that existing policies' dismissal and Also-resolve still work.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A caller without Read on the request sees neither its Signal nor its Decision Record (list and by id; same 404 as unknown); an external caller with a grant on a related record sees neither; a reader meeting an unknown subject table fails closed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`--filter "FullyQualifiedName~Signals"` passes with the baselines updated in this change; the Intake filter and full tests/Spaarke.ArchTests pass; build 0 warnings.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No log line, ProblemDetails, Signal text or Decision Record text contains document text or the reject reason.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Rewritten 2026-11-28 after the first run stopped at its escalation trigger (no Decision Record kind for intake; no create-once Work Item). Owner chose the Decide lane; conditions from ontology-r1 and uac-r2 are in notes/decisions.md. PR description must name the base and the three ontology areas (Services/Signals, Api/Signals, catalog) this branch changes; ontology-r1 reviews those, uac-r2 reviews access. Running the policy seed script on dev needs the owner's go. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</notes>

